KG42.register("clusters-b858b020e88d405707d7546e",{"id":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v142-d-CL003","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","label":"SES price response and energy-purchase balance after capacity allocation","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL003","label":"SES price response and energy-purchase balance after capacity allocation","market_meaning":"After capacity allocation, the buyer arranges energy purchases and SES charging/discharging according to electricity prices, subject to meeting the current energy gap. The energy-purchase objective and the current-period energy balance provide interfaces for the response behavior, and the aggregator's equipment operation responsibility serves as institutional background; the existing Rule-Chain cannot yet provide a closed intertemporal dispatch.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["coordination","activation","clearing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"That capacity has been allocated and the current energy gap has been met are behavioral preconditions in the source text; this is not used to add execution orders such as purchasing energy first and then charging. Low price and high price retain qualitative meanings, and no unique price or threshold is specified. The responsibilities of the aggregator operating the equipment and the buyer choosing the strategy are retained separately.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"This Rule-Cluster centers on intertemporal energy-use response after the allocated right to use energy storage, and has input conditions, buyer strategy activities, and energy-storage use results that are independent of bilateral clearing. The shared energy-purchase and balance Rule-Chain only provides interfaces, and the capacity-allocation mechanism itself still lacks upstream records.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the behavioral conditions for charging at low prices, discharging at high prices, and meeting the current gap after capacity allocation."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Connect to the same buyer's objective of choosing P2P or grid energy purchase based on price, without recounting it as an independent energy-purchase rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"shared","role":"support","rationale":"Cite the buyer energy balance, charging and discharging quantities, and their existing domains, supporting the quantity interface for meeting current-period demand."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"shared","role":"context","rationale":"Only indicate the institutional background that the aggregator is responsible for SES operation; this is not used to determine that it chooses the charging and discharging strategy on behalf of the buyer."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e002","v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E15"],"rationale":"The source text places the buyer's price-based energy purchase and adjustment of SES charging and discharging within the same energy-use management scope, supporting a joint interpretation; a general electricity-price signal is not directly equated with a particular bilateral price or a fixed threshold."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-pbc","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-pbd","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E21"],"rationale":"The qualitative condition for meeting the current gap connects to the buyer balance containing energy purchase, charging, and discharging. R003 has no quantity declaration of its own, so only an interface between behavior and existing quantities is established, and no variable is fabricated."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-L003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-e003","v141-b-g02-e002","v141-b-g02-e006"],"rationale":"The same SES is operated by the aggregator and its use is arranged by the buyer according to price, explaining institutional responsibility and user behavior respectively. This background correspondence does not constitute a new dependency in which the aggregator optimizes the buyer's strategy or forcibly dispatches."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-M001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g02-e006"],"rationale":"In the same buyer-behavior explanation, the source text uses electricity prices to coordinate energy purchase and the SES strategy; the two places refer to the same price-signal coordination function node. This display choice is not equivalent to distinct electricity-price quantities, nor does it merge the two activity constraints."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B citations for SES behavior, buyer balance, and operation responsibility have not yet been independently audited, and the current assembly is only an experimental candidate.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e002","v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e003"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the user-behavior conditions, equipment responsibility, and corresponding mathematical constraints; do not describe candidate-support eligibility as verification of source correctness."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G002","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The node proposals for capacity allocation and energy-storage physical operation remain pending. Although the R001 variable domain retains the charging and discharging power bounds, mutual exclusion, efficiency, energy-storage state and energy bounds, initial state, and shared-capacity conditions have not formed a closed dispatch in the frozen constraint catalog; capacity allocation and fairness also do not have corresponding complete Rule-Chains.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-pbc","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-pbd","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-pu","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e015","v141-b-g02-e017","v141-b-g02-e027"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-X01","v141-b-g01-X02","v141-b-g02-p001"],"required_work":"Manually decide how to handle the ontology of the proposals, and then upstream should complete the records of capacity-use rights and physical operation according to the actual source text; this round does not insert new nodes or add state constraints."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G003","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The existing behavioral citations do not define thresholds for low and high prices, a unique electricity-price convention, or a response function, so a computable optimal charging and discharging strategy cannot be derived from the qualitative description.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-rho","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-lambda_buy"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e002","v141-b-g02-e006"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check whether the source text provides specific price choices and response definitions; if not, retain the qualitative behavioral scope and use the completed optimization and energy-storage constraints to determine the numerical strategy, without setting thresholds on one's own."}]},"rule_refs":["49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R003","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R004","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R001","49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R002"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-3cc1c6ed2324280e","COMP-4c1817f6cddf8a9c","COMP-58a3c8caf66a5d40","COMP-820ecd8f4d709ac7","COMP-d063772d8846dd91","COMP-da34359f040da554","COMP-e49253a62f66ee53"]});
